\f1\fs22 Exasperated, Dunhilton stabbed his tablet with his middle finger, which fired up the conference room holo screen. \'91Can anyone tell me how this guy thinks he can upstage the Very Arch Business Bishop of tax-damned Ulyssia?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A holo-vid resolved on the middle of the board table. The image shook and blurred, as if the device capturing proceedings was being jostled amid a mob. It steadied and focusses on the back of an ornately dressed Elvi strolling up an aisle in what quickly became familiar to those in the room as the nave of St Hedges Cathedral. They saw the look of disdain as the Very Arch Business Bishop looked down upon the distasteful hospitality clone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Exasperated murmurs filled the boardroom as the holo-vid projected the High Elvis swaggering up the nave of St. Hedges Cathedral, his sequined cape shimmering with an audacious defiance that verged on blasphemy in such an austere space. As the Archbishop d\'92Molesto\'92s expression turned from disdain to barely concealed panic, the room of cabinet directors erupted into comments laced with incredulity, observation, and, on occasion, grudging admiration.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Where did he even find that cape?\'94 the Director of Moral Observance fluttered, his tone scandalized yet tinged with envy. \'93No clone from the Ghetto should be allowed to outshine the sanctity of gold-threaded robes.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It\'92s not the cape,\'94 Defence muttered darkly, leaning toward the holo-vid as if the pixels might yield military intelligence. \'93Look at the sunglasses and jewellery. They\'92re deflecting beams from the stained glass directly onto the congregation. See that glittering haze? That\'92s intentional.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As if on cue, the light shifted through one of the cathedral's immaculate stained glass windows, casting refracted beams against the sequins of the High Elvis's jumpsuit. Small specks of bluish and golden light exploded across the nave, a celestial burst mirrored in the dark sunglasses of the gathered Elvi. Far from alarmed, the clones gazed upward in near-religious awe, their faces illuminated by the spectacle. The camera briefly adjusted focus to capture their fervent expressions, mouths agape as though witnessing the literal descent of a deity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I couldn\'92t believe this,\'94 Dunhilton hissed, stabbing the table with his index finger for emphasis, though his words were practically drowned out by the recording of the chanting crowd. \'93The Very Arch Business Bishop being upstaged by a hospitality clone in a cape and discount sunglasses.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Discount?\'94 Tourism sneered, folding his arms smugly. \'93Those sunglasses probably cost more than most Ghetto homes. They\'92re designer. Look at the reflectivity\'97custom work. You can\'92t buy those off a Floormart shelf.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93STOP COMMENTING ON HIS WARDROBE!\'94 Dunhilton thundered, silencing the murmurs. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It\'92s psychological warfare,\'94 Gerry muttered, resisting further indulgence in the absurdities. \'93The spectacle undermines the solemnity of the event while elevating clone morale. Every beam of light, every glittering reflection\'97it all reinforces the Elvi\'92s sense of purpose. It\'92s propaganda.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The holo-vid zoomed closer as the High Elvis finally reached the dais, where the Very Arch Business Bishop sat frozen, halfway through rising indignantly from his throne. For a charged moment, localised in the hazy glow that enveloped them, the High Elvis stood tall beside the Bishop, deflecting the authority of the official with a studied bow of his head that inexplicably felt like mockery. The cavernous hall, now speckled with swirls of coiling light, paused as though the physical universe itself debated who deserved dominance in this tableau.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92ll say this much,\'94 Defence noted dryly, \'93whatever decorum d\'92Molesto could claim had no defence against geometrically correct rays of light playing disco on his ornate plasterwork. He looks defeated.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And defeated d\'92Molesto appeared. A shift in the light mercifully tempered the High Elvis\'92s perceived divinity, but the damage was done. The Elvi in the pews began to chant rhythmically, \'93Holy Momma! Holy Momma!\'94 The holo-vid captured d\'92Molesto\'92s thinly concealed horror as the cathedral walls quaked with their fervor. The Bishop adjusted his robes and stepped toward the pulpit, only for the High Elvis to take a confident step forward and reach for the gilded staff traditionally reserved for ceremonial blessings.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This is where he crosses the line,\'94 Tourism remarked with a whistle, clearly enjoying the carnage unfolding on-screen.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the recording ended with the chants intensifying into thundering applause, Dunhilton stared down the room, his frustration evident. His voice softened, laced with venomous determination. \'93What we just witnessed was a calculated, deliberate attack on the dignity of our Airborne institutions. A hospitality clone dared to rival the vicar of capitalism itself and walked away with the crowd\'92s faith. This ends now. Give me actionable solutions, not sycophantic commentary. Are we gods, or are we whittled to shadows?\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The reminder of their fragile standing sent shivers through the directors, each recalibrating their inward ambitions as the ramifications of such a spectacle loomed darker than the brief brilliance of refracted light on sequins.\

